  "brief": "Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery have completed their acquisition, creating a new global entertainment leader called Skydance, after a legal battle.\n\nParamount / Warner Bros. Discovery (Completed): Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery Deal Completed. Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery have completed their acquisition, creating a new global entertainment leader called Skydance [1, 2, 3]. The deal brings CNN and CBS under one owner, with the new company combining studios, streaming services, and cable networks [4, 5]. The acquisition was officially completed on Tuesday, after a legal battle [6, 7, 8].\nWittington Investments / Boots (Announced): Wittington Investments Acquires Boots. Wittington Investments is acquiring Boots for $8.9 billion [12, 13, 14]. The deal was announced on October 7 [12, 13, 14].\nViatris / Pacira BioSciences (Announced): Viatris to Acquire Pacira BioSciences. Viatris is acquiring Pacira BioSciences for $1.65 billion [15, 16]. The deal will expand Viatris' non-opioid pain therapy offerings [15, 16]. Viatris will become a leader in non-opioid pain therapies after the acquisition [17].\nThird Coast Bancshares, Inc. / Great Plains (Announced): Third Coast to Buy Great Plains. Third Coast Bancshares, Inc. is buying Great Plains [18, 19, 20]. The deal is valued at about $240M [18]. The companies have announced the deal [19].\nSpaceX / Nvidia (Rumored): SpaceX and Nvidia Deal Rumors. SpaceX is reportedly seeking to acquire Nvidia's chip business [21, 22, 23]. Apollo and banks are in talks to finance the deal [24, 25]. The deal is reportedly worth $40 billion [21, 22, 24]. SpaceX is seeking $40 billion in financing to make the purchase [26, 27, 28].\nNiccol's / Chipotle (Rumored): Niccol's and Chipotle Deal Rumors. Niccol's and Chipotle are reportedly in a deal [29]. The deal is still in the rumored stage [29]. No new information is available [29].\nBending Spoons / Eventbrite (Pending approval): Eventbrite Sold to Bending Spoons. Eventbrite is being sold to Bending Spoons [30]. The deal is pending regulatory approval [30]. No further information is available [30].\nAkzoNobel / Axalta (Pending approval): AkzoNobel and Axalta Deal. The deal is between AkzoNobel and Axalta [31]. The deal is pending approval [31]. Nippon Paint is acquiring AkzoNobel's Southeast Asia decorative paints business [32, 31].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- The Business Journals reported that the Bay Area captured one-third of U.S. startup acquisitions [33].\n- Kyiv Post reported that Kushner's aide Dmitriev discussed US investor stake in sanctioned Nord Stream Pipeline with sources [34].\n- Mexico Business News reported that Mexico bets on tech to enhance industrial platforms [35].",
